3051:          "body": "[Local Codex: code-review] Bind Goto confirmation to the selection and access that opened it\n\nReviewed head: 8698a1e640ca70fcbeb43f1eddbd04ca2aa0718b\n\nThe time-restriction dialog callback reads the current selection and checked sessions when it closes. It is not canceled on a route or access transition. If the operator opens it for group A, switches to group B, selects a block there, and then confirms the old dialog, testCommandGoto sends a command to B using the time confirmed for A. A selection change within the same group has the same problem.\n\nRemedy: Capture the intended selection, target IDs, group and access scope when opening the dialog; cancel the confirmation and pending command on route, access or component teardown, and reject changes to the captured context.\n\nStatic review; not claimed as a browser reproduction.",
3054:          "status": "open",
3087:          "body": "[Local Codex: code-review] Do not repeatedly cancel slow Booklet enrichment\n\nReviewed head: 8698a1e640ca70fcbeb43f1eddbd04ca2aa0718b\n\nEach five-second snapshot replaces the entire Booklet-enrichment observable with switchMap. Booklet requests use ref-counted sharing, so if a Booklet takes longer than the snapshot interval, each new snapshot unsubscribes and aborts the preceding read before it can populate the cache. A consistently six-second Booklet response can therefore prevent rows from ever rendering despite the 20-second HTTP deadline. The focused slow-snapshot test covers the snapshot request, not this subsequent enrichment.\n\nRemedy: Keep in-flight Booklet reads alive across snapshot replacements or coordinate snapshot and enrichment work so it can finish within the existing deadline; retain cancellation on disconnect and access changes.\n\nStatic review; not claimed as a browser reproduction.",
3090:          "status": "open",
3123:          "body": "[Local Codex: code-review] Handle absent Booklet states and options when sorting\n\nReviewed head: 8698a1e640ca70fcbeb43f1eddbd04ca2aa0718b\n\nThe state-column list is the union of states from all displayed Booklets, but the comparator dereferences each row's state definition and selected option whenever that row has any bookletStates object. A row with a different Booklet, an unset state, or an outdated option makes this throw. The error propagates through the subscription into the sessions BehaviorSubject, terminating monitor updates instead of sorting the rows.\n\nRemedy: Resolve each state and option defensively, including the defined default where appropriate, and use a stable fallback for missing or obsolete values. Add coverage for mixed Booklets and partially populated state objects.\n\nStatic review; not claimed as a browser reproduction.",
3126:          "status": "open",
3159:          "body": "[Local Codex: slop-review] Finish-all excludes pending tests from the lock request\n\nReviewed head: 8698a1e640ca70fcbeb43f1eddbd04ca2aa0718b\n\nThe confirmation says the action locks and ends all tests in the session, but the captured lock target list excludes every session whose state is pending. The native snapshot can contain pending tests with valid test IDs, and the selected-lock endpoint accepts those IDs. After the remaining requests succeed, the UI returns to the chooser, leaving those pending tests unlocked.\n\nRemedy: Include eligible pending tests in the captured lock targets, while continuing to restrict termination commands to appropriate connected tests. Add a finish-all case containing both pending and running tests and verify their resulting lock states.\n\nStatic review; not claimed as a browser reproduction.",
